This directory is owned by one contributor at a time. Two agents editing it concurrently already
destroyed a round of applied migrations.

Rules that are now enforced by scripts/verify-migration-history.mjs (runs in verify-all.sh and CI):
  1. An applied migration file is append-only. Never edit or delete one — add a new migration.
  2. Two migrations may not share a numeric prefix.
  3. Every .sql file must be recorded in CHECKSUMS.json; after adding a new migration run
     `node scripts/verify-migration-history.mjs --record`.
Changes to guard functions, triggers or the seed belong in a NEW migration, not in an edited old one.
